/T (Early opportunities would be more likely to include generic medicines, medical consumables and final-stage processing than advanced biologics. Pharmaceutical transit would also support specialised industries such as refrigerated transport, laboratory certification, customs brokerage, digital tracking, secure warehousing and backup power. Many of these capabilities would benefit the wider economy: cold storage could serve agricultural exports, tracking systems could support other manufacturing supply chains, and improved electricity and fibre connectivity would reduce costs across multiple sectors.)
